<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 26.25 trln lire BOTs.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy seen issuing 26.25 trln lire BOTs.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian Treasury is expected on average to issue 26.25 trillion lire worth of short-term bills (BOTs) at auction on June 25 against 31.5 trillion worth of paper maturing, analysts polled by Reuters said.</p>
<p>The Treasury is also expected to offer 2.0 trillion lire of 18-month zero coupon certificates (CTZs) together with 3.5 trillion lire of 24-month CTZs.</p>
<p>At end-June, CTZs for a total of 8.649 trillion lire mature. The 18-month CTZ to be offered will be new paper maturing on December 30, 1998 while for the 24-month certificates the Treasury is expected to reopen the May 1999 CTZ.</p>
<p>The Treasury will detail the amounts on offer on Friday, while settlement for the paper is on June 30.</p>
<p>Following are the analysts' forecasts (in trln lire):</p>
<p>		 3-Mo     6-Mo     12-Mo    Total    18-Mo   24-Mo</p>
<p>		 BOT	BOT	 BOT	BOT	CTZ     CTZ</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------- BankAmerica  8.5     10.0	8.0     26.5	2.0	4.0</p>
<p>BancaRoma    8.5     10.0	9.0     27.5	2.0	4.0</p>
<p>Caboto	 9.0	9.5	8.5     27.0	3.5	2.0</p>
<p>BCI	    8.5	9.5	8.5     26.5	2.0	3.5</p>
<p>Chase	  8.0	9.0	8.0     25.0	2.0	3.0</p>
<p>Credito	8.0     10.0	8.5     26.5	2.0	4.0</p>
<p>Indosuez     9.0	9.5	8.5     27.0	2.0	2.5</p>
<p>Prometeia    8.0	8.0	8.0     24.0	  * 8.0 *</p>
<p>================================================================ CONSENSUS    8.5	9.5	8.25    26.25     2.0	3.5</p>
<p>Maturing    10.0     11.5     10.0     31.5	  -	8.649</p>
<p>================================================================</p>
<p>* Prometeia's CTZ forecast if for the whole month of June.</p>
